{
  "id": "latent-factor",
  "term": "latent factor",
  "definition": "A latent factor is an underlying dimension that is not observed directly but is inferred from the pattern of correlations among survey items. In factor analysis, items that cluster together are treated as indicators of the same latent factor, which researchers interpret and label as a dimension of the construct being measured.",
